			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Delegate remaining Vine notification atoms to Vine crate\n\nFollowing the systematic modularization of the Mountain backend, replace the remaining local gRPC notification handlers in `Source/Vine/Server/Notification/` with delegation shims pointing to the dedicated `Vine` crate.\n\nThis migration covers the implementation logic for `ApplyTextEdits`, `DebugLifecycle`, `RegisterCommand`, `SetTextEditorDecorations`, and the complete `StatusBar` notification suite. The complex manual batching logic for command registration and text editor decorations—previously implemented via local `mpsc` channels and flusher tasks in Mountain—is now handled centrally by the `Vine` library namespace.\n\nAdditionally, modularize the provider unregistration atoms for authentication, debug adapters, and file systems by delegating to the `::Vine::Server::Notification` namespace. The Mountain-side modules are reduced to thin pass-throughs that satisfy the gRPC service interface while leveraging the library's standardized IPC handling and logging.\n\nThis change completes the extraction of Cocoon → Mountain notification logic, significantly pruning the internal code surface of the Mountain element and enforcing consistent IPC standards across the project.",
			"SHA": "40295339347ace07332b14935ab775793e792d53"
		},
